# SPP bid date 2026-08-17 — long/short calls

**Run basis.** `bid_dt` = 2026-08-17. The most recently cleared DA is 2026-08-16's (the 8/17 DA had not posted at run time), so "DA side" below means 8/16's cleared DA used as the proxy for what the market says binds. Real RT evidence is 8/15 in full plus 8/16 hours 1–8. 25 candidates, 8 on the DA side, 19 binding in RT.

**Attribution PDF window: 2026-08-07 → 2026-08-13.** It stops three days short of the bid date. 24 sections, and only **4 of 25 candidates** appear in it (`lnfulton_c-pat_wx`, `lnksc10-farb`, `lnmdwst-frnkln1`, `lnstilwell-redel5`, plus `xfmrnowst1-nowst1_rev23` as a name variant of `xfmrnowst1-nowst1`). For the other 21 there is no write-up and the calls fall through to outages, RT and zonal evidence. Nothing below presents a stale write-up as describing tomorrow.

**Tomorrow's zonal setup (median percentile, on-peak / off-peak):**

| Zone | wind on/off | load on/off | |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 54 / **6** | 35 / 21 | off-peak wind floor |
| 2 | **9 / 0** | 45 / 45 | wind floor both peaks |
| 3 | **9 / 4** | **77** / 40 | wind floor, load firm (hrs 15–20 at 83–93 pct) |
| 4 | **0 / 3** | 41 / 48 | wind at the absolute floor hrs 15–24 |
| 5 | 37 / 30 | 29 / **9** | |
| 21 | 48 / 38 | **9 / 0** | load floor |

The single dominant fact tomorrow is **system-wide low wind** — zone 4 on-peak wind sits at the 0th percentile, zones 2 and 3 in the bottom decile. Load is only middling (zone 4 at 41–48), firm only in zone 3. That combination rewards constraints that bind on thermal redispatch and punishes anything that needs a wind push or a peak-load day.

