## Gaps

- **PDF is 3 days stale and covers 4 of 25 candidates.** 21 candidates have no attribution at all; their calls rest entirely on outages, RT record and zonal fit. `xfmrnowst1-nowst1` matched only via the `_rev23` name variant — I read it deliberately rather than letting it fall through as "NOT IN PDF."
- **15 of 25 candidates fell back to zone 4** because the sheet has no mapping, so their lift was measured against the wrong zone's forecast — **low-confidence attribution** for: ln6_me4-sw51, lnaurorawa-flandru, lnbrook_ln-junctn5, lnbrookngs-aurorawa, lncommtap4-bois_tap, lnfulton_c-pat_wx, lnhoyt-54mr, lnjeff-aubu, lnksc10-farb, lnmanfl7-clec_pel, lnmdwst-frnkln1, lnseminole-maud_tap, lnsiouxfl-moodyco, xfmrlex1611-lex1611, xfmrmidj-midj. Several of these are clearly not zone 4 — brookngs/aurorawa/flandru are WAUE-NSP, fulton_c-pat_wx is CSWS, manfl7-clec_pel is CLECO. Where the PDF names a zone I used it (CSWS for fulton, OKGE/WFEC for mdwst-frnkln1) and noted the disagreement.
- **`linked_outages` returned only 4 rows for 25 candidates.** Tier-1 outage matching for the other 21 is my own cross-reference of `sched_outages` by element name against the contingency string — reliable for Split Rock–White, Mustang–SW 5th, Pittsburg–Valliant, Hoyt–Northland and Saline–Knoll1; fuzzier for Haysville Tap–Midland WR against `xfmrmidj-midj`.
- **`lnaurorawa-flandru`'s lift is statistically thin** — baseline 0.0005 over 17,496 hours means the 16.5× figure comes off roughly 9 binding hours.
- **The 8/17 DA had not cleared at run time**, so the "DA side" throughout is 8/16's cleared DA standing in for it.
- **Sheet's latest `bid_date` is 2026-08-16**, one day behind the bid date; 1,209 rows, 59 zone mappings. No row exists for 8/17 yet.
- **No uplift failures and no forecast holes** — all 25 candidates returned a lift, and all 6 zones × 24 hours are populated for 8/17.

Housekeeping deleted 8 stale scratch files and 1 run log; no PDFs touched. Nothing was written to the bidding sheet.
